<!--
  BlockML Core — bootstrap documentation

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.documentation.DocumentationModel
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:blockml="org.blockml.bml"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:lang="org.blockml.bml.language"
  xmlns:relation="org.blockml.bml.relation"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <idea>Block documentation model — idea, documentation, references, examples, README, documentation blocks.</idea>

  <documentation>
    Every root block definition carries a documentation model at the definition site — single
    source of truth inside BML files:

    idea (required, first child) — semantic meaning of the Block; the stable constant (WOT: Idea).
    summary (optional) — short prose expansion between idea and documentation; inherited from
      StructuralDefinition on blocks and members.
    language (optional) — natural language for documentation prose; inherits Library → Block
      default (English on org.blockml.bml.core.Block).
    documentation (required on root blocks) — technical description of the Block definition itself;
      optional language attribute when prose deviates from effective block language.
    not (optional, blocks only) — what this Block is not; block-level disambiguation from similar concepts.
    Member elements carry their own summary and documentation for individual Properties, Aggregations, etc.

    Optional extensions (wherever documentation is permitted):
    since — version from which the element is available
    changelog — container of change entries (oldest first)
    examples — container of example entries (title in block natural language + CDATA body)
    references — container of see entries (block, file, or url + relationship text)

    Natural language inheritance (documentation prose and example titles):
    Library.language → Block.language → documentation / change / see language attribute
    Unqualified names inside &lt;language&gt; and on documentation, change, and see language=
    resolve via org.blockml.bml.language.*. Authors declare language only when deviating from
    the effective inherited language. Example title language always follows the enclosing block — example
    language attribute applies to CDATA content only (implementation dialect: OpenSCAD,
    TypeScript, …) and also resolves via org.blockml.bml.language.*.

    Authoring split:
    • documentation carries technical prose only
    • references carries all cross-links — Blocks, Definition elements, repository markdown
      files, and external URLs — each with an explicit relationship note
    • Do not repeat cross-links in documentation prose

    see target attributes — exactly one target kind:
    block="core:ValueType" — Block or Definition type via xmlns prefix
    file="02_mbml.md" — repository documentation file
    url="https://…" — external URL
    property="com.foo.Bar.properties.width" — PropertyDefinition canonical path
    aggregation="com.foo.Bar.aggregations.parts" — AggregationDefinition canonical path
    association="com.foo.Bar.associations.parent" — AssociationDefinition canonical path
    capability="com.foo.Bar.capabilities.render" — CapabilityDefinition canonical path
    Split form: block="com.foo.Bar" property="width" → com.foo.Bar.properties.width in BOM.

    relation attribute (optional) — Block reference to org.blockml.bml.relation.*; unqualified
    names resolve via implicit namespace org.blockml.bml.relation.*. Omitted =
    org.blockml.bml.relation.SeeAlso. Standard blocks: SeeAlso, ReadFirst, Extends, Requires,
    ContrastsWith, AuthoringGuide, Defines, DeepDive.

    README blocks (baseType org.blockml.bml.core.Bootstrap) are library entry points for humans
    and LLMs. Curated reading order is expressed via references with relation=ReadFirst — not via
    a separate readFirst aggregation on Bootstrap. Documentation blocks
    (org.blockml.bml.documentation.*) inherit from org.blockml.bml.core.Documentation.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="02_mbml.md">
      idea, summary, not, documentation, since, changelog, examples, references — authoring rules.
    </see>
    <see file="16_framework_base_types.md">
      Definition branch documentation model — StructuralDefinition sub-blocks.
    </see>
    <see file="12_bom_object_model.md">
      DocumentationExample, DocumentationReference — BOM documentation shapes.
    </see>
    <see file="01_system.md">
      V2 documentation migration — Markdown vs BML roles.
    </see>
    <see block="lang:NaturalLanguage">
      Natural language branch — documentation prose and example titles.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Block">
      Root block — documents idea, language, documentation, references on every definition.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Definition">
      Definition branch — shared documentation aggregations.
    </see>
    <see block="def:StructuralDefinition" relation="Defines">
      Documentation property and Change, Example, Reference sub-blocks on StructuralDefinition.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Relation" relation="Defines">
      Relation branch — optional relation attribute on see entries.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Documentation">
      Abstract base for narrative documentation blocks in readFirst lists.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Bootstrap" relation="Defines">
      Abstract bootstrap role marker — ReadFirst lives on references, not on Bootstrap.
    </see>
    <see block="blockml:README" relation="SeeAlso">
      Standard README entry point — references with relation=ReadFirst in learning order.
    </see>
    <see block="relation:ReadFirst" relation="Defines">
      Relation block for curated bootstrap reading path entries.
    </see>
    <see block="doc:BootstrapModel">
      Next reading step — README.bml, readFirst, bootstrap context.
    </see>
  </references>

  <name>DocumentationModel</name>
  <type>
    <doc:DocumentationModel />
  </type>
  <baseType>
    <core:Documentation />
  </baseType>
</block>
